<title>HUNGARY: MOL GROUP DOUBLES OP PROFIT IN JAN-SEPT.</title>
<headline>MOL GROUP DOUBLES OP PROFIT IN JAN-SEPT.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine-month period ending Sept</p>
<p>30, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>					 Jan-Sept 96    Jan-Sept 95</p>
<p>    Group operating profit     13,571.1   vs    6,871.0</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit	 12,678.4   vs    3,911.3</p>
<p>    Group after-tax profit     11,054.7   vs    2,149.8</p>
<p>    Group net sales	     332,816.3   vs  231,700.6</p>
<p>    Group other revenue	   6,288.1   vs    4,518.9</p>
<p>    Material expenditures     210,914.2   vs  141,907.5</p>
<p>    Personnel expenditures     25,074.4   vs   19,031.9</p>
<p>    Depreciation		   21,262.6   vs   23,099.0</p>
<p>    Other costs		    16,057.1   vs    9,555.2</p>
<p>    Other expenditures	   54,897.9   vs   39,396.8</p>
<p>    Net financial income	    892.3 loss vs 3,218.3 loss</p>
<p>     Financial revenue	    4,770.5   vs    2,028.2</p>
<p>     Financial expenditure	5,662.9   vs    5,246.5</p>
<p>    Net extraordinary income	  0.4 loss vs   258.5 profit</p>
<p>     Extraodrinary revenue	  698.7   vs    3,761.9</p>
<p>     Extraordinary expenditure    699.0   vs    3,503.4</p>
<p>    Taxation			  1,623.7   vs    1,761.5</p>
<p>NOTE - MOL is an oil and gas company. The figures are</p>
<p>consolidated and are calculated according to Hungarian</p>
<p>Accounting Standards.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
</text>
